1. Definitions

"Licensor" means Danyil Grypak.

"Software" means the source code, object code, documentation and other
material in this repository, in every version published here on or after
2 October 2026.

"Official Build" means a build of the Software that the Licensor distributes,
for example through the App Store, Google Play or the Licensor's own website,
together with everything such a build installs, builds or runs on your devices
and servers as part of its normal operation.

"Contribution" means a change to the Software that you submit to the Licensor
under CONTRIBUTING.md.

2. What you may do without a license

(a) Read the Software, and view and fork it on GitHub as GitHub's Terms of
    Service allow.
(b) Download the Software to read it, to review its security, or to report a
    problem to the Licensor.
(c) Copy, modify, compile and run the Software privately, only to prepare,
    test and submit a Contribution. A build made for this purpose may not be
    used for anything else, and may not be shared with anyone other than the
    Licensor.
(d) Quote short excerpts for commentary, review or discussion, with
    attribution.

3. What needs a commercial license

Everything not allowed by section 2 needs a separate written license from the
Licensor. This includes, for personal and for business purposes alike:

(a) compiling, building or packaging the Software, except as section 2(c)
    allows;
(b) installing, running or using the Software, or any build or modified
    version of it that is not an Official Build;
(c) copying, publishing, distributing, selling, renting, sublicensing or
    hosting the Software or any build of it, or offering it as a service;
(d) making or distributing modified versions or derivative works, except a
    Contribution;
(e) removing or bypassing any license check, payment or activation in the
    Software.

To buy a license, write to license@gryonix.com.

